Currently, private climate finance is tracked through a range of monitoring tools and strategic analytical mechanisms, including: 
The Ukrainian Sustainable Fund operates a platform supported by the IRF and the EU that lists and assesses green financing instruments in Ukraine, including current private and public-private mechanisms, and forecasts their potential;
The C4CA (Capacity for Climate Action) project / Ukrainian Climate Office helps to identify investment opportunities, MRV gaps, stimulate investors through training and analytics;
The Ministry of Economy, together with the DiXi Group think tank and the Green Transition Office, has developed a digital catalog "Green Platform", which contains data on over 60 green financing programs for businesses, communities and enterprises.
It is also worth noting the international initiative Climate Finance Tracking Program, which provides an overview of finance flows for decarbonization and adaptation. This initiative systematically collects data on the volume of public and private financing, including Ukraine, and annually publishes relevant reports and analytical reviews.
